There shall be a Planning and Zoning Commission consisting of nine members. For further reference, see: Title 6, Chapter 1 of the City Code of Ordinances of the City of Wrens, Georgia.
3.1.1 Appointment and Terms of Commission Members.
(a) Commission members shall be appointed by the City Council. Members shall serve five year staggered terms and may continue until their successors are duly appointed. The City Council shall have the right to remove any member of the Commission for cause.
(b) The Commission shall annually elect one of its members as Chairman.
3.1.2 Meetings of the Commission.
(a) The Commission shall establish a regular meeting schedule. It has only advisory authority, reviewing and making recommendations to the City Council on zoning and land development matters. Thus, the Commission shall conduct its meetings so as to obtain necessary information and to provide a forum for public participation.
(b) Minutes shall be kept of all Commission proceedings.
(c) All Commission meetings shall be open to the public. Whenever feasible the agenda for each meeting shall be made available in advance of the meeting.
3.1.3 Quorum and Voting.
(a) A quorum for the Commission shall consist of a majority of its membership (excluding vacant seats). A quorum is necessary for the Commission to take official action.
(b) All actions of the Commission shall be taken by a majority vote, a quorum being present.
3.1.4 The Powers and Duties of the Commission.
(a) Specific Limitation of Powers: The Commission does not have the power to: amend any zoning ordinance or subdivision regulations; rezone any land; declare this Ordinance or any amendment thereto invalid; or allow any use not permitted by this Ordinance.
(b) The duties of the Commission shall include:
(1) Recommending to the City Council changes in the Unified Development Ordinance that the Commission believes are appropriate;
(2) Recommending to the City Council approval, disapproval or other action on all requests for Zoning Changes as provided in this Ordinance;
(3) Recommending approval or denial of a Conditional Use permit after a public hearing;
(4) Hearing and deciding appeals where it is alleged by the appellant that there is an error in any order requirement, decision or refusal made by the Building Inspector or Zoning Administrator or other administrative official in the administration or enforcement of any provisions of this Ordinance;
(5) Approving or denying applications for Variances from the development requirements of this Ordinance;
(6) Approving or disapproving Preliminary Plats for land subdivisions;
(7) Dispensing general information about this Ordinance to the public upon request;
(8) Reviewing questions involving interpretation of the City's Zoning Map, including zoning district boundary lines and lot lines;
(9) Advising the City Council on matters of zoning and land development as it may deem appropriate;
(10) Conducting such other business and affairs as may be, from time to time, requested by the City Council.

