6.3.1 Purpose. The City finds that it is in the best interest of the health, welfare, safety and morals of the community to enact regulations to reduce the possible adverse impacts of adult entertainment establishments. However, the City also finds that the outright prohibition of such establishments could improperly infringe upon protected forms of expression. Therefore, the purpose of this Ordinance is to reasonably regulate adult entertainment establishments in a manner that serves the legitimate governmental interest of reducing criminal activity and protecting property values without unreasonably infringing upon the protected rights of adult entertainment establishments and their patrons. For further reference, see: Title 7, Chapter 8 of the City Code of Ordinances of the City of Wrens, Georgia.
6.3.2 Location of Adult Entertainment Establishments. Adult Entertainment Establishments are restricted to the following locations:
(a) Adult Entertainment Establishments shall only be located within a A-1A District.
(b) No Adult Entertainment Establishment shall be located within 1,000 feet of any of the following:
(1) Any parcel of land which is either zoned or used for single or multi-family uses or purposes;
(2) Any parcel of land upon which a church, school, licensed day care center, governmental building owned or operated by a government, library, civic center, public park, playground, hospital, nursing home or community club is located;
(3) Any parcel of land upon which another Adult Entertainment Establishment is located;
(4) Any parcel of land upon which an establishment selling alcoholic beverages is located.
6.3.3 Site Requirements.
(a) The minimum lot area for an Adult Entertainment Establishment shall be one acre with a minimum 120 feet of road frontage on a public right-of-way;
(b) Buildings and structures established in connection with an Adult Entertainment Establishment shall be set back at least 50 feet from any property line;
(c) Merchandise or activities of the establishment shall not be visible from any point outside the establishment.
6.3.4 Permitted Uses. (See Table of Permitted Uses - Article 8). Adult Entertainment Establishments (See: Section 2.1.7).
6.3.5 Accessory Uses. All Accessory Uses permitted in C Commercial Districts.
6.3.6 Conditional Uses. Only those Conditional Uses provided for in Article 8 of this Ordinance are permitted in a A-1A District. Conditional Uses are subject to the approval of the City Council and those conditions listed in Article 18.

