(a) An application for a building permit shall be made in writing to the Building Inspector on forms provided by the City to the property owner or the property owner's agent. It is the sole responsibility of the property owner to assure that the building permit has been properly issued. The application shall be accompanied by the Building Permit Application Fee. It shall be unlawful for the Building Inspector to approve the plans or issue a building permit for any excavation or construction until he has reviewed and inspected the application and related plans in detail and found them to be in conformity with this Ordinance.
(b) Site Plan: An application for a building permit shall be accompanied by a site plan, drawn to scale, showing:
(1) A copy of the plat of survey prepared by an Engineer or Surveyor;
(2) The actual shape, location, and dimensions of the lot to be built upon;
(3) The shape, height and location of building(s) or structure(s) to be erected or altered on the lot;
(4) The sizes, locations, and use of all existing buildings or structures on the lot;
(5) A statement describing the intended use of the building(s) or structure(s) to be erected or altered;
(6) The number of dwelling units the building, if residential, is designed to accommodate;
(7) The layout of off-street parking and unloading spaces;
(8) Signature of the Jefferson County Health Officer approving the proposed location of a septic tank and field lines, provided public sewerage is not available;
(9) Identification of the type of soil the dwelling or structure will be built upon (certain soils will require a soil bearing pressure test to be performed prior to permit issuance);
(10) Such other information concerning the lot or adjoining lots as may be useful in determining whether the provisions of this Ordinance are being observed.
(c) Interpretation of Ordinance: In interpreting and applying the provisions of this Ordinance, the building permit applicant shall be held to the minimum requirements for the promotion of health, safety, welfare, morals and convenience of the general welfare. The lot or yard areas required by this Ordinance for a particular building shall not be diminished and shall not be included as part of the required lot or yard areas of any other building. The lot or yard area of buildings existing at the effective date of this Ordinance shall not be diminished below the requirements herein provided for buildings hereafter erected or altered, and such required areas shall not be included as part of the required areas for any building hereafter erected.
(d) Issuance: Prior to a permit being issued by the Building Inspector for the erection, moving, alteration, renovation, enlargement or construction of any building or structure or use of premises, the plans and intended use shall indicate conformity in all aspects to the provisions of this Ordinance. If a building permit is refused, the Building Inspector shall state the reasons for such refusal in writing. A copy of the Building Inspector's written refusal shall be provided to the applicant. The Building Inspector shall not issue any permit if the land or building as proposed to be used, constructed or altered would be in violation of any provision of this Ordinance or any codes, laws or statutes of the City, the State of Georgia, or the United States of America.
(e) Duration of Permit Validity: Once issued, the building permit shall become invalid if the work authorized by the permit is suspended or abandoned for a period in excess of six months, unless a written extension is granted by the Building Inspector.

