In order to promote the safety of motorists and pedestrians and to minimize traffic congestion and conflict, the following regulations shall apply:
(a) Vehicular ingress/egress from properties to streets shall not exceed 30 feet in width;
(b) No more than two points of vehicular ingress/egress from a property to each abutting public street shall be permitted for lots with a road frontage of 100 feet or more. Lots with less than 100 feet of frontage shall have no more than one point of ingress/egress to any one public street;
(c) No point of ingress/egress shall be allowed within 35 feet of the right-of-way line of any street intersection;
(d) No curbs on City streets or right-of-ways shall be cut or altered for ingress/egress without approval of the City;
(e) An ingress/egress driveway shall not be located closer than ten feet to the nearest edge of another such driveway on the same street;
(f) The Zoning Administrator may permit, depending on safety issues and traffic use, a point of ingress/egress within 35 feet of the right-of-way line of a street intersection.

