(b) For purpose of this section, "usable open space" means an area that:
(1) Is not encumbered with any structure or dwelling;
(2) Is not devoted to use as a street, parking area or sidewalk;
(3) Is left in its natural or undisturbed state if wooded, except for the cutting of trails for walking or jogging, or if not wooded at the time of development, is landscaped for ball fields, picnic areas or similar facilities;
(4) Is capable of being used and enjoyed for purposes of informal, unstructured recreation and relaxation;
(5) Is legally and practically accessible to the residents of the development or to the public if dedication of the open space is required;
(6) Consists of land having no more than twenty five percent (25%) of its area located within a floodplain or floodway.
(c) Subdivided residential developments of less than twenty-five (25) single-family dwelling units are exempt from the requirements of this Section unless the City agrees that it will accept an offer of dedication of such open space, and in that case the offer of dedication shall be made.

